\ Compare the OLD small-day sauce input with the NEW signed-wide one.
\ These checks stop before the expensive 46-drop sauce itself. They
\ prove that the wide integration writes the same five ingredients on
\ all six previously known short-day examples.
\ No native CAL execution has occurred.

The reference sauce input is a sauce question.
The wscimmensedigits is a wide quantity.
The wscfoundationdigits is a wide quantity.

To compare native and wide sauce inputs:
  Answer the example.
  Copy the example into the sauce input.
  \ Copy the five sauce inputs field by field. CAL does not provide
  \ a built-in record-to-record Put for the sauce question type.
  Put the sauce input's calculation count into the reference sauce input's calculation count.
  Put the sauce input's requested count into the reference sauce input's requested count.
  Put the sauce input's distance count into the reference sauce input's distance count.
  Put the sauce input's sum count into the reference sauce input's sum count.
  Put the sauce input's direction count into the reference sauce input's direction count.
  Convert the example's calculation day into the converted signed day result.
  If the native widening succeeded is not 1,
    put "Failed to widen the native calculation day." into the check report; exit.
  Put the converted signed day result into the wide calendar example's calculation day.
  Convert the example's requested day into the converted signed day result.
  If the native widening succeeded is not 1,
    put "Failed to widen the native requested day." into the check report; exit.
  Put the converted signed day result into the wide calendar example's requested day.
  Answer the wide calendar example.
  Copy the wide calendar example into the sauce input.
  If the sauce input's calculation count is not the reference sauce input's calculation count,
    put "Wide and native sauce calculation counts differ." into the check report; exit.
  If the sauce input's requested count is not the reference sauce input's requested count,
    put "Wide and native sauce requested counts differ." into the check report; exit.
  If the sauce input's distance count is not the reference sauce input's distance count,
    put "Wide and native sauce distances differ." into the check report; exit.
  If the sauce input's sum count is not the reference sauce input's sum count,
    put "Wide and native sauce count sums differ." into the check report; exit.
  If the sauce input's direction count is not the reference sauce input's direction count,
    put "Wide and native sauce directions differ." into the check report; exit.

